  "id": "leakage",
  "term": "leakage",
  "definition": "In this biological context, leakage refers to bile escaping from the cut liver surface or a biliary stump after hepatectomy. It is described as a clinically important postoperative complication that can increase morbidity, prolong drainage and hospital stay, and lead to further intervention.",
